.TH MINI-BROWSER 1 "October 2026" "Mini Browser 0.2.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mini-browser \- a small native GNOME web browser
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mini-browser
.RI [ URL " or " "search terms" ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Mini Browser opens one page per resizable portrait window, with a native
GNOME header bar. Each command-line argument opens a separate window.
Quote search terms containing spaces. Without arguments, the start page opens.
It contains an address/search field and tiles for recently opened sites.
The header bar's gear button opens Settings, including Chrome data import.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage information.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the application version.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Ctrl+L
Open the address and search dialog.
.TP
.B Alt+Home
Return to the home page.
.TP
.B Ctrl+,
Open Settings.
.TP
.B Ctrl+N / Ctrl+W
Open a new window / close the current window.
.TP
.B Alt+Left / Alt+Right
Navigate back / forward.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+I
Import Chrome bookmarks and history.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+P
Manage the encrypted password vault and import Chrome password CSV files.
New vaults use an exactly six-digit PIN. Existing vaults accept their old
master password, which can be changed to a PIN in the Passwords dialog.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+L
Choose and fill a saved login for the current website.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+K
Lock the password vault.
.TP
.B F1
Show all keyboard shortcuts.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/mini-browser/
Personal library, encrypted vault, cookies, and website data.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/mini-browser/
Website cache.
.PP
XDG_DATA_HOME and XDG_CACHE_HOME override the default data and cache roots.
.SH SEE ALSO
Documentation is installed in /usr/share/doc/mini-browser/.
